cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use these aggregate results, cite BCI Report and the release you used,
  and cite the upstream dataset each figure was computed on: every dataset page
  at https://bci.report/datasets/ gives its credit line. The licence below,
  CC BY 4.0, covers the aggregate measurements this project produced
  (LICENSE-DATA); the underlying recordings keep their own terms. The code in
  the repository is under the MIT License (LICENSE).
type: dataset
title: "BCI Report: public EEG decoding results reported with their protocol"
abstract: >-
  Cohort-level EEG decoding results, each published with the protocol that
  produced it — cohort, electrode count, evaluation split, chance level,
  interval and known limitations — across motor imagery, SSVEP, P300 and
  semantic ERP, cognitive load, sleep staging (including simple baselines on
  healthy and sleep-apnoea cohorts, kept apart, with accuracy beside balanced
  accuracy), idle false activation and non-control rejection, when a decoder
  should decline to decide (rejection rules and probability calibration
  compared as methods, not as deployment error rates), sensor and
  display transfer, image-rate transfer, movement, calibration budget within a
  recording and across sessions, decoders trained on a person's earlier
  session and tested on a later one (including a negative result in
  continuous cursor tracking), frozen probes of further EEG foundation models
  with each dataset checked against the authors' published pretraining lists,
  foundation-model adaptation (head only, last block, LoRA), one shared
  representation answering several questions (fixed heads against
  question-conditioned heads and separate models, at matched data and compute),
  pretraining controls and a clinical case/control comparison. No
  raw EEG, no per-participant scores, no overall ranking.
